@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Step down when frames drop
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Frontend — Ride app (world library, lazy)" #E0F2FE
  participant "WorldScene" as scene
  participant "WorldRenderer" as renderer
  participant "FrameBudget" as budget
end box
scene -> renderer : start(…, { tier, stepDown })
renderer -> budget : new FrameBudget(level, period, { pinned: stepDown is false })
loop each drawn frame
  renderer -> budget : sample(now, frame time)
  alt two 2 s windows in a row over 1.2 × the period, and not pinned
    budget --> renderer : drop: next lower level, or Low at 3 × (L2-159 AC4)
    renderer -> renderer : applyTier() for the rest of the ride (L2-160 AC3)
  else step-down off (pinned)
    budget --> renderer : keep, however slow (L2-160 AC2)
  end
end
note over scene : A new quality object with the same scale and cap restarts nothing:\nthe budget's windows are restarted only by a new frame period.
@enduml
